cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this
  file. The accompanying manuscript is currently under review for the
  Scientific Data "10 Years of FAIR" special issue; a full article citation
  will be added here once it is published (see also README.md).
title: "How did data sharing evolve in the decade since the FAIR Principles?"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Samuel
    given-names: Sheeba
    email: sheeba.samuel@informatik.tu-chemnitz.de
    affiliation: >-
      Distributed and Self-organizing Systems, Chemnitz University of
      Technology, Chemnitz, Germany
  - family-names: Mietchen
    given-names: Daniel
    email: daniel.mietchen@fiz-karlsruhe.de
    affiliation: >-
      FIZ Karlsruhe - Leibniz Institute for Information Infrastructure,
      Berlin, Germany; Institute for Globally Distributed Open Research and
      Education (IGDORE), Göteborg, Sweden
abstract: >-
  Code, notebooks, and pipeline for a large-scale longitudinal analysis of
  data-sharing practice in biomedical articles from the PubMed Central Open
  Access Subset (2011-2025), relative to the 2016 publication of the FAIR
  Guiding Principles.
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/myVSR/fair-data-sharing-evolution"
keywords:
  - FAIR principles
  - data sharing
  - data availability statements
  - open science
  - reproducibility
  - PubMed Central
